{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01To3vYR7bsbCgwiZ8XHysgz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Anchor R&D Surface v5 â€” \"Durable Work\" â€” Master Plan (frozen design)\n2\t\n3\t> Crucible Stage 1 output, locked 2026-06-14. Builds on the v4.1 \"Project Cockpit\"\n4\t> (merged): clean Paradigm-2 project window (tile board â†’ inline panels with split\n5\t> summary + terminal), engine toggle, grass idea board, deliverable launch-by-type,\n6\t> flat dashboard rows, Option B branding, plus the terminal fixes (full-width fit,\n7\t> Ctrl+V paste, no-freeze pump). v5 makes the surface **durable and resumable**:\n8\t> sessions don't vanish, past work opens to a real summary you can continue, ideas\n9\t> are a filterable two-pane workbench, every build has a listed deliverable, and\n10\t> project summaries actually say what the project is for.\n11\t\n12\t## North Star (locked)\n13\t\n14\tMake every R&D session and idea a **durable, resumable, well-summarized unit of\n15\twork**. Closing a session never loses it (it stays a reopenable tile); a *separate*\n16\tdeliberate action kills it. Opening a past session shows a **real summary** â€” the\n17\tskill invoked, the prompts asked, the actions/files produced â€” with one click to\n18\t**continue it in a fresh live session** seeded from that context. The Grass Catcher\n19\tis a **filterable two-pane idea workbench**: ideas carry stable ids and a\n20\trawâ†’refinedâ†’promoted status, are developed in-place with Research/Plan, versioned,\n21\tand pulled into other efforts. **Every Foreman build has a clearly identified\n22\tdeliverable**, listed both in the Deliverables lane and inside that build's panel.\n23\tAnd the **project summary** on the dashboard row and project header conveys the\n24\tproject's actual objective/purpose â€” not boilerplate.\n25\t\n26\t## Why v5 (what's wrong today, from live use)\n27\t\n28\t1. **Closing a run destroys it.** X on a session panel removes it entirely â€” a\n29\t   started research run vanished. There's no \"keep it around to reopen\" vs.\n30\t   \"deliberately kill it\" distinction.\n31\t2. **A past session is a dead end.** Opening a done/historical session shows only\n32\t   \"session complete\" â€” no sense of what it did, and no way to pick it back up.\n33\t3. **Project summaries are uninformative.** The one-liner (row) and project-header\n34\t   summary don't capture the project's objective/task/purpose.\n35\t4. **Foreman builds have no visible deliverable.** A build runs but no deliverable\n36\t   is identified or listed â€” neither in the Deliverables lane nor in the build's\n37\t   own panel.\n38\t5. **The Grass Catcher is thin.** It needs to be a real idea workbench (filter by\n39\t   status, switch between ideas fast, develop an idea with a tool, version and pull\n40\t   refinements into efforts).\n41\t\n42\t## Locked decisions (Stage 0/1 user gates)\n43\t\n44\t1. **Run lifecycle = close-to-tile vs. deliberate kill.** The panel's **X closes\n45\t   the panel but KEEPS the session as a reopenable tile** (the session/record\n46\t   persists; a running session keeps running; a done one stays done). A **separate,\n47\t   clearly-distinct control hard-KILLS** the session (terminate + remove worktree +\n48\t   drop the tile), behind an \"Are you sure?\" confirm. The two are visually and\n49\t   behaviorally distinct; closing must never lose work.\n50\t2. **Past-session view = real summary + continue-live.** Opening a done/historical\n51\t   session shows a summary: **the skill invoked, the prompts/turns asked, and the\n52\t   actions/files produced** (built from the session's transcript/log + member docs,\n53\t   through the validated `summarizer` seam â€” cached, generate-once). A **\"Continue\n54\t   in a live session\"** button starts a NEW live terminal session in the same lane,\n55\t   **seeded with that session's context** (its summary/transcript), so the user can\n56\t   pick the work back up. Reuses the Wave-1 seed path (`terminal_session.start_session`\n57\t   with `seed_context`).\n58\t3. **Better project summaries.** Improve `summarizer.summarize_project`: a stronger\n59\t   seed (CLAUDE.md / README / Anchor.md + newest plan docs + pinned deliverables +\n60\t   lane activity) and a prompt that extracts the **objective/task/purpose** in 1â€“2\n61\t   sentences, grounding-filtered. Cached (generate-once on rescan; `force`\n62\t   regenerates). The dashboard row + project header READ the cache; never a\n63\t   synchronous model run on render.\n64\t4. **Deliverable per Foreman build.** Every Foreman build run resolves a\n65\t   **deliverable** (the artifact it produced â€” from the run's output / pinned path /\n66\t   `foreman.config` `docs`/declared marker). **Backfill:** scan existing build\n67\t   sessions per project and resolve their deliverables. List deliverables in the\n68\t   **Deliverables lane** AND inside each **Build session's panel**. When a build\n69\t   genuinely has no resolvable deliverable yet, say so honestly (\"no deliverable\n70\t   pinned yet\") â€” never fabricate one.\n71\t5. **Grass Catcher = B+C hybrid workbench** (approved mockup\n72\t   `_mockups/grass_catcher_refined.html`): a **filter-tab row** (All / raw / refined\n73\t   / promoted [+ search]) over a **two-pane workbench** â€” idea list left, the\n74\t   selected idea's workbench right (idea text + **Develop: Research / Plan** in the\n75\t   workbench terminal + engine toggle + **Promote to a lane**). Ideas carry stable\n76\t   ids (`grass-<hash>`) and a **rawâ†’refinedâ†’promoted** status; refinements are\n77\t   **versioned** (`grass-<id>/dev-N`), logged, and **pullable into other efforts**;\n78\t   a **promoted** idea links to the run it became. **Project-scoped** (a\n79\t   cross-project Grass view is out of scope for v5). Developing happens in the\n80\t   workbench terminal (with a \"Promote to a lane\" when an idea graduates).\n81\t6. **Terminal vertical resize is already shipped** (v4.1 fit fix) â€” v5 only adds a\n82\t   guard test; no rework.\n83\t7. **Verification standard (non-negotiable, baked into every UI wave).** \"Done\" for\n84\t   any UI change = **rendered-DOM assertions** (parse the served HTML, positive AND\n85\t   negative) **+ a real Playwright/Chromium interaction test** (click the thing,\n86\t   assert the result) **+ a screenshot the orchestrator visually checks against the\n87\t   mockup** **+ the user's sign-off before merge**. A string-grep test is NEVER\n88\t   sufficient. This is the lesson from v4 (a vacuous gate shipped a broken UI).\n89\t8. **Scope = one Foreman build** on `C:\\dev\\Anchor`, every wave GREEN on\n90\t   `python -m pytest -v`.\n91\t\n92\t## Inclusion test (the size rule)\n93\t\n94\tEvery wave serves a North-Star criterion. **Out of scope** (bloat / later):\n95\tcross-project Grass view, a full transcript replay/scrubber (a summary suffices),\n96\tre-architecting the summarizer pipeline (extend it), multi-user, and any change to\n97\tthe proven terminal substrate beyond what items above require.\n98\t\n99\t## Hard constraints (from CLAUDE.md â€” non-negotiable)\n100\t\n101\t- **Python stdlib only**, except the declared lazy `pywinpty` (in `pty_manager.py`\n102\t  only). **Playwright is a DEV-ONLY test dependency** (`pytest.importorskip`), never\n103\t  imported by product code; `distro.py`'s import scan must stay green.\n104\t- **Never bind/touch the live `:8777` service or real data in tests/healthcheck.**\n105\t  Model calls via `tests/fake_claude.py` (`ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD`); PTY via the stub\n106\t  backend (`ANCHOR_PTY_BACKEND=stub`); any spawned preview/service on an OS-assigned\n107\t  port **HARD-guarded `!= 8777`** with an isolated temp `ANCHOR_DATA_DIR`.\n108\t- **All mutating / terminal / launch endpoints** behind the `do_POST` token gate;\n109\t  GET read-only (token via `?token=`).\n110\t- **f-string brace discipline** in `anchor_gui.py` (`_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS` is a RAW\n111\t  single-brace string; doubled braces in f-string HTML/CSS).\n112\t- **Mirror** new data seams into `anchor.py`; **extend** `anchor_healthcheck.py`\n113\t  (`check_rnd_v5_surface`, fully stubbed); **update** `CLAUDE.md`.\n114\t\n115\t## Risks & mitigations\n116\t\n117\t- **R1 â€” \"keep as tile\" leaks running PTYs.** Closing a panel must not kill the PTY,\n118\t  but a killed/closed-then-forgotten running session shouldn't run forever.\n119\t  Mitigation: closing keeps the registry record + tile; the session reconciler\n120\t  already re-statuses dead sessions; hard-kill is the explicit reap. Test: close\n121\t  keeps the record + a live PTY; kill reaps it with no orphan.\n122\t- **R2 â€” continue-live duplicates/!diverges work.** Continue seeds a NEW session\n123\t  (new worktree) from the prior summary; it does not mutate the original. Test:\n124\t  continue starts a fresh session seeded with the prior context; original intact.\n125\t- **R3 â€” summary fabrication.** Both session and project summaries go through the\n126\t  generate-twice + grounding filter; ungrounded claims dropped; honest \"no\n127\t  metrics\"/\"no deliverable\" when data is absent.\n128\t- **R4 â€” deliverable backfill mis-identifies.** Resolve from explicit signals\n129\t  (pinned path / config docs / declared marker / known build output) only; when\n130\t  ambiguous, list \"unresolved â€” pin one\" rather than guessing.\n131\t- **R5 â€” another vacuous UI gate.** Mitigated by Locked Decision 7 (Playwright +\n132\t  screenshot + sign-off mandatory per UI wave).\n133\t\n134\t## Definition of done (project)\n135\t\n136\tAll waves GREEN on `python -m pytest -v`; closing a session keeps it as a reopenable\n137\ttile and a separate control hard-kills it; a past session opens to a real summary\n138\t(skill + prompts + actions) with a working \"continue in a live session\"; project\n139\tsummaries convey the objective on the row + header; every Foreman build's deliverable\n140\tis listed in the Deliverables lane and its build panel (honest when none); the Grass\n141\tCatcher is the B+C hybrid workbench (filter tabs + two-pane + develop terminal +\n142\tversioned/pullable refinements + promote links + search); the CLI mirrors the new\n143\tseams; `check_rnd_v5_surface` passes fully stubbed; `distro` scan clean; CLAUDE.md\n144\tupdated; and every UI wave is verified by Playwright + a screenshot + user sign-off.\n145\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f0f0cb9-60a0-484b-896f-92ece53a4401","uuid":"a48ef04d-c164-4985-a7c6-dcf78bb7d70c","timestamp":"2026-06-14T21:57:42.273Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Anchor\\planning\\rnd-v5\\MASTER-PLAN.md","content":"# Anchor R&D Surface v5 â€” \"Durable Work\" â€” Master Plan (frozen design)\n\n> Crucible Stage 1 output, locked 2026-06-14. Builds on the v4.1 \"Project Cockpit\"\n> (merged): clean Paradigm-2 project window (tile board â†’ inline panels with split\n> summary + terminal), engine toggle, grass idea board, deliverable launch-by-type,\n> flat dashboard rows, Option B branding, plus the terminal fixes (full-width fit,\n> Ctrl+V paste, no-freeze pump). v5 makes the surface **durable and resumable**:\n> sessions don't vanish, past work opens to a real summary you can continue, ideas\n> are a filterable two-pane workbench, every build has a listed deliverable, and\n> project summaries actually say what the project is for.\n\n## North Star (locked)\n\nMake every R&D session and idea a **durable, resumable, well-summarized unit of\nwork**. Closing a session never loses it (it stays a reopenable tile); a *separate*\ndeliberate action kills it. Opening a past session shows a **real summary** â€” the\nskill invoked, the prompts asked, the actions/files produced â€” with one click to\n**continue it in a fresh live session** seeded from that context. The Grass Catcher\nis a **filterable two-pane idea workbench**: ideas carry stable ids and a\nrawâ†’refinedâ†’promoted status, are developed in-place with Research/Plan, versioned,\nand pulled into other efforts. **Every Foreman build has a clearly identified\ndeliverable**, listed both in the Deliverables lane and inside that build's panel.\nAnd the **project summary** on the dashboard row and project header conveys the\nproject's actual objective/purpose â€” not boilerplate.\n\n## Why v5 (what's wrong today, from live use)\n\n1. **Closing a run destroys it.** X on a session panel removes it entirely â€” a\n   started research run vanished. There's no \"keep it around to reopen\" vs.\n   \"deliberately kill it\" distinction.\n2. **A past session is a dead end.** Opening a done/historical session shows only\n   \"session complete\" â€” no sense of what it did, and no way to pick it back up.\n3. **Project summaries are uninformative.** The one-liner (row) and project-header\n   summary don't capture the project's objective/task/purpose.\n4. **Foreman builds have no visible deliverable.** A build runs but no deliverable\n   is identified or listed â€” neither in the Deliverables lane nor in the build's\n   own panel.\n5. **The Grass Catcher is thin.** It needs to be a real idea workbench (filter by\n   status, switch between ideas fast, develop an idea with a tool, version and pull\n   refinements into efforts).\n\n## Locked decisions (Stage 0/1 user gates)\n\n1. **Run lifecycle = close-to-tile vs. deliberate kill.** The panel's **X closes\n   the panel but KEEPS the session as a reopenable tile** (the session/record\n   persists; a running session keeps running; a done one stays done). A **separate,\n   clearly-distinct control hard-KILLS** the session (terminate + remove worktree +\n   drop the tile), behind an \"Are you sure?\" confirm. The two are visually and\n   behaviorally distinct; closing must never lose work.\n2. **Past-session view = real summary + continue-live.** Opening a done/historical\n   session shows a summary: **the skill invoked, the prompts/turns asked, and the\n   actions/files produced** (built from the session's transcript/log + member docs,\n   through the validated `summarizer` seam â€” cached, generate-once). A **\"Continue\n   in a live session\"** button starts a NEW live terminal session in the same lane,\n   **seeded with that session's context** (its summary/transcript), so the user can\n   pick the work back up. Reuses the Wave-1 seed path (`terminal_session.start_session`\n   with `seed_context`).\n3. **Better project summaries.** Improve `summarizer.summarize_project`: a stronger\n   seed (CLAUDE.md / README / Anchor.md + newest plan docs + pinned deliverables +\n   lane activity) and a prompt that extracts the **objective/task/purpose** in 1â€“2\n   sentences, grounding-filtered. Cached (generate-once on rescan; `force`\n   regenerates). The dashboard row + project header READ the cache; never a\n   synchronous model run on render.\n4. **Deliverable per Foreman build.** Every Foreman build run resolves a\n   **deliverable** (the artifact it produced â€” from the run's output / pinned path /\n   `foreman.config` `docs`/declared marker). **Backfill:** scan existing build\n   sessions per project and resolve their deliverables. List deliverables in the\n   **Deliverables lane** AND inside each **Build session's panel**. When a build\n   genuinely has no resolvable deliverable yet, say so honestly (\"no deliverable\n   pinned yet\") â€” never fabricate one.\n5. **Grass Catcher = B+C hybrid workbench** (approved mockup\n   `_mockups/grass_catcher_refined.html`): a **filter-tab row** (All / raw / refined\n   / promoted [+ search]) over a **two-pane workbench** â€” idea list left, the\n   selected idea's workbench right (idea text + **Develop: Research / Plan** in the\n   workbench terminal + engine toggle + **Promote to a lane**). Ideas carry stable\n   ids (`grass-<hash>`) and a **rawâ†’refinedâ†’promoted** status; refinements are\n   **versioned** (`grass-<id>/dev-N`), logged, and **pullable into other efforts**;\n   a **promoted** idea links to the run it became. **Project-scoped** (a\n   cross-project Grass view is out of scope for v5). Developing happens in the\n   workbench terminal (with a \"Promote to a lane\" when an idea graduates).\n6. **Terminal vertical resize is already shipped** (v4.1 fit fix) â€” v5 only adds a\n   guard test; no rework.\n7. **Verification standard (non-negotiable, baked into every UI wave).** \"Done\" for\n   any UI change = **rendered-DOM assertions** (parse the served HTML, positive AND\n   negative) **+ a real Playwright/Chromium interaction test** (click the thing,\n   assert the result) **+ a screenshot the orchestrator visually checks against the\n   mockup** **+ the user's sign-off before merge**. A string-grep test is NEVER\n   sufficient. This is the lesson from v4 (a vacuous gate shipped a broken UI).\n8. **Scope = one Foreman build** on `C:\\dev\\Anchor`, every wave GREEN on\n   `python -m pytest -v`.\n\n## Inclusion test (the size rule)\n\nEvery wave serves a North-Star criterion. **Out of scope** (bloat / later):\ncross-project Grass view, a full transcript replay/scrubber (a summary suffices),\nre-architecting the summarizer pipeline (extend it), multi-user, and any change to\nthe proven terminal substrate beyond what items above require.\n\n## Hard constraints (from CLAUDE.md â€” non-negotiable)\n\n- **Python stdlib only**, except the declared lazy `pywinpty` (in `pty_manager.py`\n  only). **Playwright is a DEV-ONLY test dependency** (`pytest.importorskip`), never\n  imported by product code; `distro.py`'s import scan must stay green.\n- **Never bind/touch the live `:8777` service or real data in tests/healthcheck.**\n  Model calls via `tests/fake_claude.py` (`ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD`); PTY via the stub\n  backend (`ANCHOR_PTY_BACKEND=stub`); any spawned preview/service on an OS-assigned\n  port **HARD-guarded `!= 8777`** with an isolated temp `ANCHOR_DATA_DIR`.\n- **All mutating / terminal / launch endpoints** behind the `do_POST` token gate;\n  GET read-only (token via `?token=`).\n- **f-string brace discipline** in `anchor_gui.py` (`_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS` is a RAW\n  single-brace string; doubled braces in f-string HTML/CSS).\n- **Mirror** new data seams into `anchor.py`; **extend** `anchor_healthcheck.py`\n  (`check_rnd_v5_surface`, fully stubbed); **update** `CLAUDE.md`.\n\n## Risks & mitigations\n\n- **R1 â€” \"keep as tile\" leaks running PTYs.** Closing a panel must not kill the PTY,\n  but a killed/closed-then-forgotten running session shouldn't run forever.\n  Mitigation: closing keeps the registry record + tile; the session reconciler\n  already re-statuses dead sessions; hard-kill is the explicit reap. Test: close\n  keeps the record + a live PTY; kill reaps it with no orphan.\n- **R2 â€” continue-live duplicates/!diverges work.** Continue seeds a NEW session\n  (new worktree) from the prior summary; it does not mutate the original. Test:\n  continue starts a fresh session seeded with the prior context; original intact.\n- **R3 â€” summary fabrication.** Both session and project summaries go through the\n  generate-twice + grounding filter; ungrounded claims dropped; honest \"no\n  metrics\"/\"no deliverable\" when data is absent.\n- **R4 â€” deliverable backfill mis-identifies.** Resolve from explicit signals\n  (pinned path / config docs / declared marker / known build output) only; when\n  ambiguous, list \"unresolved â€” pin one\" rather than guessing.\n- **R5 â€” another vacuous UI gate.** Mitigated by Locked Decision 7 (Playwright +\n  screenshot + sign-off mandatory per UI wave).\n\n## Definition of done (project)\n\nAll waves GREEN on `python -m pytest -v`; closing a session keeps it as a reopenable\ntile and a separate control hard-kills it; a past session opens to a real summary\n(skill + prompts + actions) with a working \"continue in a live session\"; project\nsummaries convey the objective on the row + header; every Foreman build's deliverable\nis listed in the Deliverables lane and its build panel (honest when none); the Grass\nCatcher is the B+C hybrid workbench (filter tabs + two-pane + develop terminal +\nversioned/pullable refinements + promote links + search); the CLI mirrors the new\nseams; `check_rnd_v5_surface` passes fully stubbed; `distro` scan clean; CLAUDE.md\nupdated; and every UI wave is verified by Playwright + a screenshot + user sign-off.\n","numLines":145,"startLine":1,"totalLines":145}}}
