ped (baseline 643+1, +8).\n31\t- **REVIEW (adversarial, prompted to refute): 1 BLOCKER** â€” a hard-killed session\n32\t  is marked `done` (terminal) but its record is kept; `repopulate()` (term_sessions\n33\t  returns every status) re-synced it into the live bar ~400ms after kill, so the\n34\t  killed chip REAPPEARED. The Playwright test raced past it (closed the browser\n35\t  before `setTimeout(repopulate,400)` fired) â†’ GREEN on broken behavior (the v4\n36\t  timing-blind-gate trap). All other 6 scrutiny points CONFIRMED-OK (close never\n37\t  reaps; kill reaps no orphan; reopen re-attaches live PTY; stdlib-only; no\n38\t  Playwright in product; never :8777).\n39\t- **FIX (orchestrator):** `repopulate()` excludes terminal-status sessions\n40\t  (`_isTerminalStatus` mirrors `session_registry.TERMINAL_STATUSES` = {done,\n41\t  failed}) from the live bar; a session that just went terminal is evicted from\n42\t  MANAGED. Strengthened the Playwright kill assertion to wait 900ms (past the\n43\t  repopulate) and re-assert the chip + panel stay gone.\n44\t- **RE-GATE (orchestrator-run, stub PTY):** 651 passed, 1 skipped. UI verified:\n45\t  rendered-DOM (positive `#sessionBar`/`#panelStack` + negative old `Ã— == kill`),\n46\t  real Playwright openâ†’closeâ†’reopenâ†’kill, and an orchestrator screenshot of the\n47\t  panel header showing the grey `Ã—` and a distinct red `ðŸ—‘` (visually confirmed).\n48\t- **COMMIT (scoped):** `dd08c6b` â€” anchor_gui.py + test_run_lifecycle.py +\n49\t  test_project_window.py only (no runtime churn).\n50\t\n51\t## Wave 2 â€” Past-session view: real summary + \"Continue in a live session\" â€” GREEN (2026-06-14)\n52\t\n53\t- **EXECUTE** (fresh sub-agent): (A) `summarizer.summarize_session` extended with\n54\t  three DETERMINISTIC source-grounded fields â€” `skill` / `prompts` / `actions`\n55\t  (read straight off session+member records, NEVER through the model â†’ zero\n56\t  fabrication; honest empty/placeholder when absent). Model `claims` still go\n57\t  through generate-twice + grounding filter; failed-runner branch still skips the\n58\t  cache (no poison). (B) Historical panel JS (`_mountReadOnlyBody` rewritten â†’\n59\t  `_renderPastSession`/`_fillPastSessionDetail`) replaces the \"session complete\"\n60\t  dead-end with skill+prompts+files+doc-role links. (C) New token-gated\n61\t  `POST /api/rnd/continue_session` (+ `_build_continue_seed`) â†’ `start_session` in\n62\t  the SAME lane seeded with the prior summary; original never mutated (R2).\n63\t- **GATE (orchestrator-run, stub PTY):** 660 passed, 1 skipped (baseline 651+1, +9).\n64\t- **REVIEW (adversarial, prompted to refute): SHIP â€” 0 BLOCKER, 2 MINOR.** All 7\n65\t  scrutiny points CONFIRMED-OK: R3 grounding intact (skill/prompts/actions are real\n66\t  reads; `frobnicate`/`zzyzx` ungrounded claims still dropped); cache generate-once\n67\t  + force + no-poison-on-failure; R2 original byte-identical after continue + fresh\n68\t  worktree; endpoint token-gated; UI gate is a REAL Playwright clickâ†’panelâ†’summaryâ†’\n69\t  continue test (NOT grep-only); stdlib-only; never :8777. MINOR: produced-file\n70\t  labels not hyperlinked (doc links live in the summary block above â€” honest, not\n71\t  dangling); handler covered via Playwright rather than a dedicated HTTP unit test.\n72\t  Neither blocks. No FIX required.\n73\t- **UI VERIFY (orchestrator):** screenshot of a discovered planning session's panel\n74\t  â€” confirmed it shows the summary header + PLAN DOCUMENTS role links + \"Skill\n75\t  invoked: not recorded\" + \"Prompts asked: none recorded\" + \"Files produced:\n76\t  Master Plan / Impl Plan\" + the blue \"â–¶ Continue in a live session\" button\n77\t  (honest placeholders for the imported case; `ro-sec`=3).\n78\t- **COMMIT (scoped):** `6b781aa` â€” summarizer.py + anchor_gui.py +\n79\t  test_session_continue.py only (no runtime churn).\n80\t\n81\t## Wave 3 â€” Better project summaries (objective/purpose) + folded dashboard ref